# RN(x) of a 2-limb number: x0 itself, since a normalized x has x0 = RN(x0 + x1).
kernel:        to_nearest_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        t
value:         x
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       rounded t nearest
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Convert.v to_nearest_2_correct
source:        the definition of normalized (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
unused:        x1 for a normalized x, x0 is RN(x) already
cone_exempt:   x1 is not used; a non-finite x1 beside a finite x0 is not a normalized operand, so the non-finite layer, which reads x0, stands in for the check

t = copy(x0)
